    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0546" n="450" xml:id="pg450"/>

                <head>No. 339.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter to Mr. Nelson.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 13,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 275.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: A copy of a letter is herewith inclosed for
                    your information, addressed by the Secretary of War to the Secretary of State on
                    the 7th instant, and transmitting the reports of Major G. W. Schofield in
                    relation to the Howard’s Well massacre.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTEE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—Since the above was written a further communication in relation to the
                        Howard’s Well massacre has been received from the Secretary of War, under
                        date of the 10th instant, and is herewith inclosed.</p>
                </postscript>









